cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Korvyr: Hybrid GNN and Static-Analysis Prototype for Pre-Install npm Package Screening"
message: "If you use this software or refer to its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mazzella
    given-names: Gianmarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/gianmarcomaz/Korvyr"
url: "https://github.com/gianmarcomaz/Korvyr"
abstract: >-
  Korvyr is a research prototype that screens npm packages before installation.
  It builds a code property graph from a package's JavaScript sources, scores it
  with a graph isomorphism network, runs a behavioural rules engine over the raw
  source and package manifest, and combines both signals into a clean,
  suspicious, or malicious verdict with supporting evidence. Reported results
  come from a single balanced 600-package development benchmark that was also
  used during policy calibration; no temporal or malware-family holdout was
  evaluated, and the corpus and trained checkpoint are not distributed with the
  repository.
keywords:
  - software-supply-chain
  - npm-security
  - malware-detection
  - graph-neural-networks
  - code-property-graph
  - static-analysis
  - pytorch-geometric
  - fastapi
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-04"
